# Beat a Path ({2}{R} Adventure of Bellowing Bruiser): "Up to two target creatures can't block this turn." (CR 509.1b, 715.) Bot2's
# Memnite and Ornithopter are both targeted: neither can block Bot1's attacking Memnite, so Bot2 takes 1.
# A third target (Bot1's own Memnite) is refused: "up to two" is at most two. A player is refused: the targets are creatures.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Memnite
Bellowing Bruiser
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Bellowing Bruiser.Cast(Ability: Beat a Path)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 19
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 2

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
